s week um to give him his  credit boris johnson took responsibility  for the tory's loss in north shropshire  when is um your leader going to take  responsibility for losing nearly  9 000  votes uh in this by-election last time  around you had more than 12 000 this  time you didn't break four thousand i  don't think we're disappointed by the  result in north shropshire well you lost  three quarters of your vote and you're  not disappointed i think it's a  significant defeat for boris johnson and  what north shropshire shows us trevor  steady steady you were second in this  seat the lib dems walked straight past  you come on  i think what north shropshire shows us  trevor is that political parties are  perfectly capable of making informed  judgments about where to spend their  resources and voters can be trusted to  make the decisions that give them the  outcome that they want in this case  removing a conservative mp and i get the  slightest bit disappointed by the result  in north shropshire okay you're  obviously having a laugh here but there  is a serious point here  doesn't this demonstrate that if you are  absolutely as serious as you purport to  be about boris johnson's failings that  the labour party the liberal democrats  the greens all now have to start  thinking if they really mean what they  say that it's time to start thinking  about an alliance that would actually  put you in power because that's the only  way to get rid of this person that you  never cease to say day in day out is not  fit to lead this country  i don't think that voters like the idea  of backroom deals and tax between  political parties i think voters are  perfectly capable of making their own  informed choices about the outcome that  they want to see  so you know looking at um the the lie of  the electoral map there will be some  parts of the country where uh getting  rid of a conservative mp the route to  that the best route to that the easiest  route to that is to vote liberal  democrat there are far more places in  the country where the route to getting  rid of a conservative mp and delivering  uh a labour government is by voting in  labor for voters voters can make more  borrowers  no i don't think that i don't think  that's a choice actually and and if  boris johnson leads the conservative  party into the next general election  more for the conservative party but  that's that's for them to worry about i  think what the labour party has shown  this week in particular but since  kiersten became leader is we've got a  serious leader with a serious team  capable of governing the country we know  we've got more work to do to win back  trust don't want to give your viewers  the impression we're in any way  complacent about this but we're  determined to do that work we're  determined to win the trust and  confidence of the people we can do that  without backroom deals and we'll put our  best foot forward and let the people  decide we're streeting thank you very  much indeed

